From 3dff66693fbba89d002c6c693fea9caf7dd4b359 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:29:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 43/45] blitz-dom: a border keeps the device pixels Stylo
 snapped it to

Stylo snaps a border's width to whole device pixels ("snap as a border
width", css-values-4): a 1px border is one device pixel at a scale of
1.25, 1.5 or 1.6, which is a fraction of a CSS pixel (0.8, 0.667,
0.617). Taffy's rounding then put each edge of the box on a whole CSS
pixel, the border's inner edges too, so such a border came out 0 or 1
CSS pixel a side by the fraction of the box's position: one side drew
nothing, another 1.6 device pixels, and with a radius and a side of 0
blitz-paint drew no border at all. At 2x the same befell a border of
one device pixel (0.5px).

set_final_layout now takes each border width from the unrounded layout,
rounded to whole device pixels at the document's scale, and keeps the
rest of the rounded layout. At 1x and 2x, where a border of whole CSS
pixels is whole device pixels too, it gives what rounding gave. At 1.6 a
2px border, 3.2 device pixels that Stylo snaps to 3, now draws 3 on
every side, as in Chromium, where rounding drew 2 CSS pixels or 1 by the
box's position. The width is rounded rather than taken as it is
because Stylo's servo device snaps in whole app units, and at 1.6 a
device pixel is 37.5 of them, so a 1px border is 37, 0.987 device
pixels.

A box's position and size, its padding and its children are where
rounding put them. Only what lies inside the border moves: the padding
box, and the content box inline text is drawn from, now start after the
border's device pixels, as in Chromium, rather than after 0 or 1 CSS
pixel. Doing it in set_final_layout covers taffy's round_layout and the
incremental rounding alike.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/mod.rs | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/mod.rs b/packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/mod.rs
index 24045c457..e2c81e736 100644
--- a/packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/mod.rs
+++ b/packages/blitz-dom/src/layout/mod.rs
@@ -959,9 +959,23 @@ impl RoundTree for LayoutPassState<'_> {
     }
 
     fn set_final_layout(&mut self, node_id: NodeId, layout: &Layout) {
+        // Rounding puts each edge of a box on a whole CSS pixel, a border's
+        // inner edges too. But Stylo has already snapped every border width
+        // to whole device pixels ("snap as a border width"), a fraction of a
+        // CSS pixel at a scale such as 1.6, and rounding the edges again made
+        // such a border 0 or 1 CSS pixel a side, by where the box sits. Keep
+        // the width on the device pixels it was snapped to. (Rounding the
+        // width, not taking it as it is, because Stylo snaps in whole app
+        // units, and at 1.6 a device pixel is 37.5 of them.)
+        let scale = self.viewport.scale();
+        let border = self.node_from_id(node_id).unrounded_layout().border;
+        let layout = Layout {
+            border: border.map(|width| (width * scale).round() / scale),
+            ..*layout
+        };
         let slot = self.node_from_id_mut(node_id).final_layout_mut();
-        if *slot != *layout {
-            *slot = *layout;
+        if *slot != layout {
+            *slot = layout;
             self.geometry_changed(dom_node_id(node_id));
         }
     }
